{"id":"u-2646ff7b-8166-471a-a344-c084390ac6cb","src":"community","title":"Combat Athlete 12 Week Program","author":"Devantw A.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/7QaS5X-the-combat-athlete","desc":"Build a stronger, faster, more explosive combat athlete over three four-week blocks. Uses basic gym equipment, free weights, bodyweight work, sprints, jumps, rotation, grip, neck training, fight conditioning, and recovery-day hip mobility. Weeks 4 and 8 deload; Week 12 tapers and tests. Workouts are designed for roughly 45–60 minutes. After Day 5, take at least one full rest day before restarting Day 1. Execution standards: assisted one-arm pull-up = shoulder-width overhand working hand; free hand grips the working wrist; alternate arms. Pull-up = shoulder-width overhand; chin-up = shoulder-width underhand. Start every pull-up or chin-up from a dead hang, finish with chin over bar, and do not kip. Muscle-up = shoulder-width overhand bar muscle-up. Towel hang = both hands on one towel. Single-arm or single-leg work, split squats, lunges, bounds, throws, chops, and Pallof presses are per side; neck holds are per direction. Follow the listed order: skill and power first, heavy compound lifts next, then assistance and conditioning. Combat circuit round = 30 seconds each of box jumps, sprawls, high knees, push-ups, mountain climbers, and burpees (3 minutes total). Hip Mobility Flow = 90/90 switches, couch stretch, adductor rock-backs, and a deep-squat hold; divide the listed time evenly.","level":["Advanced","Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Strength","Muscle","Bodyweight Fitness"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-21T10:57:08.952Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["1 - Upper Strength + Grip","2 - Sprint Jump Rotation","3 - Recovery Durability","4 - Lower Strength + Neck","5 - Explosive Power Fight Engine"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Assisted One-Arm Pull-Up","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":5,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Pull